{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>For you felt about all, etc.</b> Meaning, even utensils that have no feeling of terafim — as you would say of utensils that are smaller than the terafim, or the metaphor being that he was searching through wrappings that he could recognize from the outside that they do not contain terafim. From this you learn that he suspected him of taking utensils." "<b>What did you find of all, etc.</b> Meaning, of all kinds of utensils of your household — similar to that into which a doubt could enter for you to say that it is yours." "<b>Set it here before, etc.</b> The intention here is that previously, when he claimed that he had come to seek the terafim, he said to him: ״Recognize what is mine and take for yourself,״ in order to make him think that he sought nothing but his terafim. But when he saw him searching and examining every single thing, he said: this is surely proof that he suspects me, as I have written above, and whoever disqualifies with a blemish is himself disqualified, and now he is setting his eyes to come with a false accusation. Therefore he said to him: <b>Set it here before my brothers and your brothers, and let them judge</b> — meaning, let signs justify. And he did not trust Laban's brothers alone, for all of them are like him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:23.084767989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}